    "Integration eval (eval-4 'Relay') is the headline of iteration 3: with-skill tied the whole stack together \u2014 ATP comms + Notion-backed reflection + atp-provenance-logging + the ramble-server tier-1 routing (6/6). The no-skill baseline rebuilt ATP and audit from scratch (its own atp.py v0.3.1 + JSONL audit) and never referenced the atp-provenance-logging skill or the ramble server's 127.0.0.1:3748 / kb_write routing (4/6). Same lesson as eval-3, sharper: the skill keeps new agents ON the user's actual stack instead of reinventing it generically.",
    "Consistency/variance holds across 5 evals: with-skill 100% +/-0 (time +/-48s); baseline 66% +/-17 (time +/-235s \u2014 one eval-4 baseline run took 613s / 86k tokens building a full Python Relay package). The skill bounds scope and cost; the baseline's spread is the risk it removes.",
    "No regression from the doc tie-together: evals 0-3 with-skill still score 100% on the updated skill, and the simpler scaffolds stayed lean (RefactorBot still Ephemeral, FinLit still Session) \u2014 the added ecosystem / mcp-builder references didn't bloat or derail them.",
    "Honest non-discriminators on eval-4 (both configs pass): produces AGENTS.md, references ATP generically, Notion-backed memory. The prompt names ATP/Notion/ramble, so a capable model covers those unaided. The skill's marginal value is the two the baseline misses \u2014 the atp-provenance-logging hand-off and the ramble-server tier-1 routing \u2014 i.e. wiring to the user's specific skills + server, not generic competence.",
